-- Tight frames and an integral standard theta function: the jet series of
-- a Weil vector is the Taylor series of its theta function; products of
-- curve theta functions along tight frames come from vectors of the finite
-- part, compatibly with translations, integral-valued, with a vacuum
-- expansion.
-- Source: grh-compact/src/New/Curve/FrameSections.lean ("This file: The
-- jet series of a Weil vector is the Taylor series of its theta function.
-- Curve theta products along tight frames: translates, jets, integral
-- values, relation to the vacuum."; Space.eq_zero_of_jetSeries_eq_zero,
-- Parameters.omega₀_mem_cmCurve_lattice,
-- Parameters.exists_finitePart_of_isTightFrame), with
-- Lib/Weil/Construction/ConjugateJetDefs.lean (Space.VacuumExpansion).
-- Encoding. The source's structure VacuumExpansion, used only through
-- Nonempty, is the predicate VacuumExpansionOf (its fields under ∃). The
-- variables of a jet series are the pairs (τ, k) of an embedding τ in the
-- CM type and a row k (spaceFockIndex). A vector γ ∈ Eⁿ acts through
-- ϱ(finVec(α⁻¹γ)) = ϱ(γ), and the value F(finVec x) is θ(ϱ(αx)F). Not
-- stated here: Space.taylor_line_eq_subst_jetSeries, Space.jetSeries_eq_prod,
-- latticeModule_cmCurve (PeriodChoiceOf states it) and norm_map_psi₀.
-- Part of the GRH blueprint (layer 5, the argument).
